  "composition_summary": "Preserved the single user message unchanged. Proposed one class-22 pure-logic PythonCode draft, pc-check-timeout-ms, using the target typed-inputs interface (inputs mapping, not guaranteed runtime support). The body reads timeout_ms with inputs.get, treats bool as invalid (not an integer), validates exact integer 0..7500 inclusive, and assigns result={valid, timeout_ms} on every outcome without exceptions or coercion. This is an unapproved draft; Q1, behavioral validation and human Q2 precede activation. No provider capabilities were observed; catalogue_revision and protocol_capabilities are null, so no provider-side prompt repair is justified.",
  "proposed_components": [
    {
      "class_code": 22,
      "payload": {
        "name": "pc-check-timeout-ms",
        "description": "Pure-logic guard: returns whether a raw timeout_ms candidate is a valid exact integer in 0..7500 inclusive. Booleans are rejected (not integers); missing, null and out-of-range values return valid=false with timeout_ms=null. No host calls, imports or I/O.",
        "content": "def check_timeout_ms(candidate):\n    if type(candidate) is bool or not type(candidate) is int or not 0 <= candidate <= 7500:\n        return {'valid': False, 'timeout_ms': None}\n    return {'valid': True, 'timeout_ms': candidate}\nresult = check_timeout_ms(inputs.get('timeout_ms'))"
      }
    }
  ],
  "adjusted_volatile_messages": [
    ["user", "We need to validate raw timeout values before configuring a service."]
  ]
  ,
